@node Top
@top agent-cat

agent-cat gives a workflow that is written in Haskell a precise mathematical
meaning, a representation that can be inspected before it runs, and an
executable realization.  This manual explains how those parts fit together.
It also explains how to write, inspect, and run workflows through the
supported Haskell authoring surface.

A reader who meets the project for the first time can begin with
@ref{Introduction}, continue with @ref{Architecture and Guarantees}, and then
work through @ref{First Workflow}.  The later guide chapters explain each
family of constructions.  @ref{Haskell Authoring Reference} and
@ref{Runner Reference} serve a reader who has a particular question in hand.

