@section Relevant public instances

The following instance families determine which ordinary values fit the
authoring classes.  They are checked against their live declarations as part of
the manual coverage gate.

@table @code
@item Says
Instances admit a spliceable @code{V}, @code{Text}, and scoped prompt pieces.
@item HasSchema
Built-in instances cover @code{()}, @code{Bool}, @code{Integer},
@code{Rational}, @code{Text}, and lists whose element type has a schema.
@item KnownSchema and KnownCode
Instances construct witnesses for every primitive and composite static schema
and for every built-in or structured answer code.
@item Gives
Call arguments admit a live @code{V} at its exact code, scoped prompt pieces as
text, and literal @code{Text}.
@item Chain
Instances build typed argument chains and typed input chains.
@item Curries
Instances curry empty tuples, handle tuples, and input-text tuples.
@item Step
Instances implement every accepted statement at its valid block stage and carry
explicit type errors for unsupported stage/construction pairs.
@end table

